INT. PICKLE FACTORY ELEVATOR - DAY

A steel freight lift. Slimy floor. A single flickering bulb. The smell of brine is overwhelming.

HARVEY (40s, hairnet, clipboard) leans on one wall, scowling at the buttons. A STRANGER (40s, windbreaker, visitor badge, big grin) stands on the other, holding a jar.

STRANGER
Great plant you've got here.

HARVEY
It's a factory.

STRANGER
Great factory.

The elevator groans. Stops. Lights dim.

HARVEY
Oh, no.

STRANGER
Is that normal?

HARVEY
It's never happened. Ever.

STRANGER
Ever?

HARVEY
Except Tuesday.

He jabs a button. Nothing. He tries again. Nothing. The man unscrews the jar and sniffs.

STRANGER
You mind if I eat one?

HARVEY
Those are the quality-control samples.

STRANGER
I'm quality control.

HARVEY
I'm quality control.

STRANGER
I mean, I'm also quality control. We're all quality.

He pops a pickle in his mouth. Crunches loudly. Harvey stares.

HARVEY
Who are you?

STRANGER
Alberto Mendes. Your new regional auditor.

HARVEY
Oh, no.

ALBERTO
Don't worry, Harvey. Your pickles are fine.

HARVEY
How do you know my name?

ALBERTO
It's on your hairnet.

The elevator lurches, then plunges a foot. Both yelp. Both grab the same railing. Both look at the jar. Alberto offers it. Harvey takes one.
